{
  "level": "a1",
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "people",
      "name": "People & family",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Learn every noun together with its article. Gender is mostly arbitrary, so the article is part of the word. der is blue, die is red, das is green.",
      "words": [
        ["Mann", "man"],
        ["Frau", "woman"],
        ["Kind", "child"],
        ["Junge", "boy"],
        ["Mädchen", "girl"],
        ["Mutter", "mother"],
        ["Vater", "father"],
        ["Bruder", "brother"],
        ["Schwester", "sister"],
        ["Freund", "friend (male)"],
        ["Freundin", "friend (female)"],
        ["Familie", "family"],
        ["Name", "name"],
        ["Leute", "people"],
        ["Mensch", "human, person"],
        ["Eltern", "parents"]
      ],
      "notes": {
        "Junge": "Ends in -e but is masculine — an exception to the usual -e-is-feminine pattern.",
        "Mädchen": "Words ending in -chen are always neuter, even for a girl.",
        "Eltern": "Plural only: die Eltern.",
        "Leute": "Plural only: die Leute."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "food",
      "name": "Food & drink",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Many nouns ending in -e are feminine (die Suppe, die Lampe). There are exceptions, so keep checking the article.",
      "words": [
        ["Brot", "bread"],
        ["Wasser", "water"],
        ["Milch", "milk"],
        ["Kaffee", "coffee"],
        ["Tee", "tea"],
        ["Apfel", "apple"],
        ["Käse", "cheese"],
        ["Ei", "egg"],
        ["Butter", "butter"],
        ["Suppe", "soup"],
        ["Bier", "beer"],
        ["Wein", "wine"],
        ["Saft", "juice"],
        ["Kartoffel", "potato"],
        ["Fleisch", "meat"],
        ["Kuchen", "cake"],
        ["Zucker", "sugar"],
        ["Fisch", "fish"],
        ["Salz", "salt"],
        ["Obst", "fruit"]
      ],
      "notes": {
        "Käse": "Ends in -e but is masculine.",
        "Suppe": "-e ending, feminine.",
        "Obst": "Usually no plural."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "home",
      "name": "Home & things",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Useful endings: -ung, -heit, -keit, -schaft and -ion are always feminine. Diminutives in -chen and -lein are always neuter.",
      "words": [
        ["Haus", "house"],
        ["Zimmer", "room"],
        ["Tür", "door"],
        ["Fenster", "window"],
        ["Tisch", "table"],
        ["Stuhl", "chair"],
        ["Bett", "bed"],
        ["Buch", "book"],
        ["Schlüssel", "key"],
        ["Auto", "car"],
        ["Tasche", "bag"],
        ["Lampe", "lamp"],
        ["Küche", "kitchen"],
        ["Garten", "garden"],
        ["Straße", "street"],
        ["Stadt", "city"],
        ["Wohnung", "apartment"],
        ["Telefon", "telephone"],
        ["Computer", "computer"],
        ["Teller", "plate"],
        ["Messer", "knife"],
        ["Gabel", "fork"],
        ["Löffel", "spoon"]
      ],
      "notes": {
        "Wohnung": "-ung words are always feminine."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "time",
      "name": "Time",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Time words show up in almost every sentence. Watch the articles: der Tag, die Woche, das Jahr.",
      "words": [
        ["Tag", "day"],
        ["Nacht", "night"],
        ["Morgen", "morning"],
        ["Abend", "evening"],
        ["Woche", "week"],
        ["Monat", "month"],
        ["Jahr", "year"],
        ["Stunde", "hour"],
        ["Minute", "minute"],
        ["Zeit", "time"],
        ["Wochenende", "weekend"],
        ["Uhr", "clock, o'clock"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "places",
      "name": "Places",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Places are often neuter or feminine. Learn the article with the place, because you will need it after prepositions.",
      "words": [
        ["Schule", "school"],
        ["Arbeit", "work"],
        ["Bahnhof", "train station"],
        ["Flughafen", "airport"],
        ["Krankenhaus", "hospital"],
        ["Restaurant", "restaurant"],
        ["Geschäft", "shop"],
        ["Markt", "market"],
        ["Bank", "bank"],
        ["Hotel", "hotel"],
        ["Park", "park"],
        ["Kirche", "church"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "body",
      "name": "Body",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Body parts are mostly masculine or neuter; die Hand and die Nase are the common feminine ones.",
      "words": [
        ["Kopf", "head"],
        ["Auge", "eye"],
        ["Nase", "nose"],
        ["Mund", "mouth"],
        ["Ohr", "ear"],
        ["Hand", "hand"],
        ["Arm", "arm"],
        ["Bein", "leg"],
        ["Fuß", "foot"],
        ["Haar", "hair"],
        ["Herz", "heart"],
        ["Bauch", "belly"],
        ["Zahn", "tooth"]
      ],
      "notes": {
        "Auge": "das Auge — an exception; most -e nouns are feminine."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "clothing",
      "name": "Clothing",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Clothing is a mix of genders — a good set to drill because there is no reliable rule.",
      "words": [
        ["Hemd", "shirt"],
        ["Hose", "trousers"],
        ["Kleid", "dress"],
        ["Schuh", "shoe"],
        ["Jacke", "jacket"],
        ["Mantel", "coat"],
        ["Hut", "hat"],
        ["Rock", "skirt"],
        ["Socke", "sock"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nature",
      "name": "Nature & weather",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Weather words are common in small talk: das Wetter, der Regen, die Sonne.",
      "words": [
        ["Sonne", "sun"],
        ["Mond", "moon"],
        ["Himmel", "sky"],
        ["Baum", "tree"],
        ["Blume", "flower"],
        ["Berg", "mountain"],
        ["Fluss", "river"],
        ["Meer", "sea"],
        ["Regen", "rain"],
        ["Schnee", "snow"],
        ["Wind", "wind"],
        ["Wetter", "weather"],
        ["Feuer", "fire"],
        ["Luft", "air"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "work",
      "name": "Work & school",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Note the -in ending for female people: der Lehrer / die Lehrerin.",
      "words": [
        ["Lehrer", "teacher (male)"],
        ["Lehrerin", "teacher (female)"],
        ["Schüler", "pupil"],
        ["Student", "student"],
        ["Arzt", "doctor (male)"],
        ["Ärztin", "doctor (female)"],
        ["Beruf", "job, profession"],
        ["Firma", "company"],
        ["Büro", "office"],
        ["Chef", "boss"],
        ["Kollege", "colleague"],
        ["Wort", "word"],
        ["Frage", "question"],
        ["Antwort", "answer"],
        ["Sprache", "language"]
      ],
      "notes": {
        "Lehrerin": "Adding -in to a masculine person word makes it feminine."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "transport",
      "name": "Transport",
      "kind": "noun",
      "intro": "Vehicles are a good test of gender: der Zug, die Bahn, das Auto, das Fahrrad.",
      "words": [
        ["Zug", "train"],
        ["Bus", "bus"],
        ["Fahrrad", "bicycle"],
        ["Flugzeug", "airplane"],
        ["Schiff", "ship"],
        ["Bahn", "railway"],
        ["Koffer", "suitcase"]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
